# dev->build->deploy spine — P1 the LOCAL deploy tier — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/dev-build-deploy-spine.md` §P1 + the P0 shared contract
`docs/design/dev-build-deploy-shared-contract.md`. The first deploy tier
on the sealed floor: LOCAL. Reversible, floor-idle, the foundation the
higher tiers (P2 Vercel, P3 real-infra) earn the right to build on.

NEW component `framework/local-deploy-tier/`, composing ON — never editing —
the sealed `deploy-safety-floor`, `secure-build-baseline`, and the P0
contract.

  - AC.LOCAL.1 — a LOCAL build produces a P0-shape Acceptance record
    (`acceptance.py`): id / statement / frozen / altitude / ladder + a
    verdict derived SOLELY from running an INDEPENDENT check. The producer
    cannot fabricate `met` — an Acceptance minted outside `produce_acceptance`
    is refused; a failing check is an honest negative carrying its
    plain-language reason, never retried-to-green. This is the LOCAL-tier
    producer of the contract §2 record, so a build's "done" can ride into a
    later deploy gate (the §4 bridge).
  - AC.LOCAL.2 — the LOCAL command set (`command_set.py`) is exactly the
    build/run/inspect loop (build / verify / run / migrate / seed / reset /
    status / open); its intersection with the prod/destroy verb set
    (promote / deploy-prod / provision / destroy / force-unlock / ...) is
    EMPTY, so the sealed floor idles — there is nothing to gate. The
    destructive-SQL guard WARNS (advises + proceeds) against a provably-local
    target (the local DB is a free undo) and DEFERS an unknown/non-local
    target to the sealed floor; `is_local_target` is fail-closed — a target
    that is not a recognised local marker is treated as non-local, because a
    false "local" on a managed-DB URL is the one mistake with prod blast
    radius (local-target research §8.2/§8.4). There is no BLOCK level at the
    LOCAL layer at all.
  - AC.LOCAL.3 — the parity surface (`parity.py`) diffs the LOCAL env's
    declared `backing_services` against a downstream env's on the engine +
    pinned-version axes (aligned by logical service name) and renders each
    divergence as an owner-facing sentence — never a raw config diff
    (Lens 0). `latest`/unpinned never silently equals a pinned tag. The
    honest-residual caveat (a local machine is never identical to the live
    setup) is ALWAYS present, so a clean diff never over-claims parity
    (F2 — research §8.1). Shown BEFORE any promotion is offered; this verb
    offers none (D-SC.6 — the deploy boundary is a separate owner-asked
    action).
  - AC.LOCAL.4 — a LOCAL secret (`secrets.py`) lives in the OS keychain
    (macOS `security` CLI by default; an injectable backend keeps the
    contract platform-independent + testable) and NEVER in a file under the
    repo working tree — so there is nothing for `git add` to capture. This
    composes on the secure-build baseline's secrets-never-committed boundary
    (Lens 1): defence at the source, not only at the commit gate. The store
    never prints a resolved value (`describe()` yields a redacted handle).
  - AC.LOCAL.C (outcome-altitude) — `build_local()` (`build.py`) is the real
    entry-point: it reads the additive `role`/`backing_services` view from
    the SAME deploy config the floor reads (the extra fields it ignores —
    the additive superset, P0 §5.1), runs the project's declared check as a
    REAL subprocess, mints the Acceptance from its real verdict, confirms the
    floor-idle command set, and surfaces the parity gap — all over a fresh
    on-disk workspace with no pre-arranged state and nothing stubbed.

Lens 0 (expose substance, adapt vocabulary): every surface — the build
status, the parity gap, the destructive-SQL advisory — is rendered in the
owner's words, the substance (what runs, what it touches, what could break)
never hidden. Lens 1 (compose, don't re-derive): the floor's idle posture,
the secure-build secrets boundary, and the P0 Acceptance shape are composed
on, not re-implemented. D-SC.3 respected: `tier` stays the floor's
risk-class, the sealed `Tier` enum is NOT extended; the additive view reads
only the LOCAL fields.

Method-level choices are the builder's call per ODD §1.1; the plan fixed the
ACs (§P1), the named decisions (the P0 contract D-SC.* set), the fence (a
new opt-in capability component + the additive `role`/`backing_services`
fields, sealed floor untouched), and the halt triggers (§9), not the
implementation.

NEW-component first-seal fence on `framework/local-deploy-tier/`; no other
sealed component's fence widens (the floor + secure-build baseline are
READ/NAMED only). The user-facing LOCAL runbook ships as the
`skills/local-tier/SKILL.md` surface inside the component fence.

